<BaseLayout title="About" description="The story behind Jaba Jerky and the people who make it.">
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>About Jaba Jerky</h1>

      <!-- TODO: replace placeholder copy with the real founding story. -->
      <p>
        Jaba Jerky started with a simple question: why should meat eaters have all the good
        road-trip snacks? We set out to make a tofu jerky with real smoke, real chew, and
        enough protein to keep you going.
      </p>

      <h2>How we make it</h2>
      <p>
        We start with organic, non-GMO tofu, press it to get the water out, and let it soak in
        our marinades overnight. Then it’s slow-smoked and dried in small batches until it has
        the texture of a proper jerky.
      </p>

      <h2>What we believe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Snacks should taste great first, and be good for you second (but still good for you).</li>
        <li>Simple ingredients you can pronounce.</li>
        <li>Packaging and sourcing that go easy on the planet.</li>
      </ul>

